Done. Read-only investigation complete — no ingestion was run and no Azure calls were made. Findings written to `spikes/pipeline-rag2/docs/ingest-config-findings.md`.

10-line summary of recommendations:
1. `ingest()` accepts `loader=`, `chunker=` AND `extractor=` together — they are independent per-call slots; loader+chunker feed Steps 1-2, extractor feeds Step 4.
2. `MarkdownLoader` DOES populate `document.elements` (flat list of header/paragraph/list/table elements with `breadcrumbs`); `StructuralChunking.chunk_document` consumes them and prefixes each chunk with its header path — the per-chunk context lever.
3. For `.md` the "no structural elements → fallback" log will NOT fire; it only triggers on empty `elements` (PDF) — so the flat-list risk is NOT a concern here.
4. MANDATORY: pass `chunker=StructuralChunking(...)` explicitly — the SDK default `SentenceTokenCapChunking` ignores `document.elements` and chunk-loses the header context.
5. Recommend `StructuralChunking` alone (zero extra LLM calls); keep `ContextualChunking(llm, base_chunker=StructuralChunking(...))` as a rate-limit-guarded alternative.
6. Ingest-level `max_concurrency` is a no-op for a single source path; set `max_concurrency=2` on `GraphExtraction` (default is 12 if omitted).
7. Two bypasses defeat per-strategy caps: `ContextualChunking._enrich_chunks` calls `abatch_invoke` with no cap, and each `abatch_invoke` builds a NON-shared per-call semaphore — so a global cap needs one shared wrapper.
8. Rate-limiter: a single process-shared `RateLimitedLLM(LLMInterface)` with `Semaphore(2)` + 10-per-60s token bucket, injected into `GraphExtraction`, `ContextualChunking`, and `GraphRAG` (concurrency=2 AND throughput=10/60s, since 2 concurrent short calls overruns it).
9. Azure wiring: `LiteLLM(model="azure/gpt-5.4-mini", api_key/api_base/api_version, timeout=1800)`, `LiteLLMEmbedder("azure/text-embedding-3-large", dimensions=1536, timeout=1800)`, `GraphRAG(embedding_dimension=1536)`, `GraphExtraction(llm, entity_extractor=LLMExtractor(llm))`.
10. Key open items: DON'T pass `num_ctx` for Azure (it's Ollama-specific and `gpt-5*` triggers the reasoning-token path — HIGH conf.); `entity_types=` on GraphExtraction is redundant with `ontology=`; verify the `gpt-5.4-mini` deployment name (LOW conf); dry-run the rate-limiter sketch on 1 chunk before full ingest.
